{"id": "EUVD-2026-103650", "enisaUuid": "a9a9852b-e07a-35dc-9aa5-2354dd3049d8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/bridge: samsung-dsim: fix TE GPIO lifetime for host attach\n\nWhen the Exynos DSI driver was generalized into samsung-dsim, the TE\nGPIO acquisition was switched from gpiod_get_optional() to\ndevm_gpiod_get_optional() while keeping the matching gpiod_put() calls.\nThat combination is wrong for a managed descriptor.\n\nHowever, dropping the puts and keeping the managed get is also wrong:\nsamsung_dsim_register_te_irq() runs from the DSI host attach callback,\nand host detach/reattach can happen without destroying the device that\nowns the managed action. A second attach would then request the GPIO\nagain without having released it.\n\nSwitch back to a non-managed gpiod_get_optional() and keep the explicit\ngpiod_put() on the request_irq() error path and in\nsamsung_dsim_unregister_te_irq().\n\n[Luca: remove unnecessary comment]", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:32", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77a43e00c57486a5212ef22d4665cafad62a5d4b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5759bbef951c39d264ac0f47daa4137d01403aea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ebffd70e4877bb7554974cf975a27872f2bb225f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b796251c3cca45a33a5c859c6818c58aa982277", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ada667890773e033d2f40dc94176e3beb930b516"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98605", "GHSA-7p9h-67r4-584r"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0187ef13-ba89-344c-9c5f-80adf5f92a90", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e7447128ca4a250374d6721ee98e3e3cf99551a6 <77a43e00c57486a5212ef22d4665cafad62a5d4b"}, {"id": "029e605f-b6e8-3584-83cf-bf25a28b0ce7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e7447128ca4a250374d6721ee98e3e3cf99551a6 <9b796251c3cca45a33a5c859c6818c58aa982277"}, {"id": "263ac9d3-a3e8-3c24-aa0a-baf1d1b4d2ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e7447128ca4a250374d6721ee98e3e3cf99551a6 <ada667890773e033d2f40dc94176e3beb930b516"}, {"id": "59f2f67b-4b7d-3fd2-b1ad-4ec55daae9fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e7447128ca4a250374d6721ee98e3e3cf99551a6 <ebffd70e4877bb7554974cf975a27872f2bb225f"}, {"id": "b0669491-5599-34b3-bba0-cfc1b47cb466", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b42e881a-081c-3f02-8695-e6d2706940a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "c72bf72c-ad21-3f95-bb8a-817c6c287521", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "ceaa6c24-8e6c-3378-ad8c-18bebc89c27d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4"}, {"id": "dbd29e60-53d3-33cb-874b-70ad2378e1c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "dc7db659-57f3-3728-86e6-2b0f98e07d78", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "eb04d189-6372-327d-849c-98c5473e7df4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e7447128ca4a250374d6721ee98e3e3cf99551a6 <5759bbef951c39d264ac0f47daa4137d01403aea"}, {"id": "fed7de0e-3309-365a-b132-d9ab7eb0f1b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cd8e2e70-67a2-3236-af19-6782b28dbfc3", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}